• **Text unchanged:** the blame usage line still goes to stdout and the config refusal still goes to stderr. Only the exit code moved.
• **No string parsing:** the fix makes handle_blame_status return 2 on a usage error, and the config arm calls the existing exit_if_nonzero(2) helper.
• Tests: the new tests in tests/integration.rs pin the exact bytes and exit codes, including the cases that should still exit 0. The in-process config edit test, which would now kill the test binary, was turned into a check that the config arm's source contains exit_if_nonzero(2); it was not deleted. Its runtime coverage moved to the binary-level tests.
• Docs: docs/src/usage/commands.md describes the new behaviour.

